<!--
Members which an instance declaration adds beyond the type of the declared child.
- AlphaType/Link is a LinkType (which defines Status); its declaration adds the mandatory variable Level,
  the optional variable Note, the optional placeholder Item<no> of ItemType and the object Inner. They are
  validated through hasLink, in addition to LinkType's own constraints. Item<no> has a fixed name part:
  a child named Item... is an instance whatever its type, so a wrong type is reported; Inner is not taken in.
- Inner's declaration adds Deep: two relationships away from AlphaType, so it is reported, not validated.
- AlphaType/Plain adds nothing: no declaration shape.
- AlphaType/Mand adds the mandatory, fully generic placeholder <Part> of ItemType: any name matches, so only
  children of ItemType count as instances; the child Other (another type) is not counted.
- AlphaType/Params adds only the mandatory placeholder variable <Param> of any value rank and data type
  (like DI's ParameterSet/<ParameterIdentifier>): it has no value shape and its name cannot be checked,
  so it gives no rule, Params gets no declaration shape and the parameter Speed is not checked.
The instance conforms.
-->
